\fs64 \cf0 Overview\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf4 Decimo provides an arbitrary-precision integer and decimal library for Mojo. It delivers exact calculations for financial modeling, scientific computing, and applications where floating-point approximation errors are unacceptable. Beyond basic arithmetic, the library includes advanced mathematical functions with guaranteed precision.\
For Pythonistas, 
\fs28 decimo.BInt
\fs32  to Mojo is like 
\fs28 int
\fs32  to Python, and 
\fs28 decimo.Decimal
\fs32  to Mojo is like 
\fs28 decimal.Decimal
\fs32  to Python.\
The core types are:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
An arbitrary-precision signed integer type 
\fs28 BInt
\fs32 \cf7 \ul \ulc7 1\cf4 \ulnone , which is a Mojo-native equivalent of Python's 
\fs28 int
\fs32 .\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
An arbitrary-precision decimal implementation (
\fs28 Decimal
\fs32 ) allowing for calculations with unlimited digits and decimal places\cf7 \ul 2\cf4 \ulnone , which is a Mojo-native equivalent of Python's 
\fs28 decimal.Decimal
\fs32 .\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
A 128-bit fixed-point decimal implementation (
\fs28 Dec128
\fs32 ) supporting up to 29 significant digits with a maximum of 28 decimal places\cf7 \ul 3\cf4 \ulnone .\

