\cf4 The auxiliary types include a base-10 arbitrary-precision signed integer type (
\fs28 BigInt10
\fs32 ) and a base-10 arbitrary-precision unsigned integer type (
\fs28 BigUInt
\fs32 ) supporting unlimited digits\cf7 \ul 4\cf4 \ulnone . 
\fs28 BigUInt
\fs32  is used as the internal representation for 
\fs28 BigInt10
\fs32  and 
\fs28 Decimal
\fs32 .\
Decimo combines "Decimal" and "Mojo" - reflecting its purpose and implementation language. "Decimo" is also a Latin word meaning "tenth" and is the root of the word "decimal".\
This repository includes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/forfudan/decimo/blob/main/docs/readme_tomlmojo.md"}}{\fldrslt \cf7 \ul TOMLMojo}}, a lightweight TOML parser in pure Mojo. It parses configuration files and test data, supporting basic types, arrays, and nested tables. While created for Decimo's testing framework, it offers general-purpose structured data parsing with a clean, simple API.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa530\partightenfactor0

\fs64 \cf0 Installation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf4 Decimo is available in the modular-community 
\fs28 https://repo.prefix.dev/modular-community
\fs32  package repository. To access this repository, add it to your 
\fs28 channels
\fs32  list in your 
\fs28 pixi.toml
\fs32  file:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf4 \cb5 channels \cf7 =\cf4  \cf7 [\cf8 "https://conda.modular.com/max"\cf7 ,\cf4  \cf8 "https://repo.prefix.dev/modular-community"\cf7 ,\cf4  \cf8 "conda-forge"\cf7 ]\cf9 \
      \cb1 \
\cb5 \
      \
    \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf4 \cb1 Then, you can install Decimo using any of these methods:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa320\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf4 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
From the 
\fs28 pixi
\fs32  CLI, run the command 
\fs28 pixi add decimo
\fs32 . This fetches the latest version and makes it immediately available for import.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In the 
\fs28 mojoproject.toml
\fs32  file of your project, add the following dependency:\uc0\u8232 
\fs28 \cb5 decimo \cf7 =\cf4  \cf8 "==0.8.0"\cf9 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf9 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
      \
